s you everything—they could see what this really was: an abuse of power meant to punish people for standing up for the Constitution. **Friend, even in this moment of intimidation and chaos, ordinary Americans still recognize the difference between the rule of law and raw political revenge.** [](https://click.actionnetwork.org/ss/c/u001.iIBo0N5fSFzEFL40Tn-vtbMETCUYClkOrOh9-SNJfqtHtWNDtXR0WReOmqZcCOXObfMgaGY5raGLc1PxOT-O68TdeN6kJLZ6Ix4mjuuc63DgIaB5VmS-ekzlTF1SM2bxMtvaiIUltj4qDjpi0mEqSEoge0Sz3fkEpOOw8zTVhSJ5XrZ7OuZqCYuB_WyLBiZ0x5CuDkl3SlBnGyOZHSaSXSV7mnDrQW2V-ySmsxNaQQV4e52iXNZcGDH6mczOmZfaME5r6h62-63LfZrBFmzg_gJMWeBwj41ag2YqS5tZGbclzkbFSAj2QJoF5eb-qvpkNzV3iYCCFWSK8J1Xm5YoZoCtoSK_zgQH6wDMTteCzA2VshWYDkIGYkkzj__Fa5Fqg9E4aIzJb596S-MOECeyWTCu1YFygSsHbNR9h_zp1Z5mg-8FmLI6XvWzQ-yK1qbu/4o9/NwQVZu5KTU-ImEHVBzyGOw/h7/h001.7eduuKM9VUbmPpxFMOCCqcuu7ja4ViEpRoCGOicETSU) I first swore an oath to the Constitution as a 17-year-old at the Naval Academy. I took that oath again when I was elected to represent Western Pennsylvania in Congress. That oath is sacred. It’s lifelong. It doesn’t expire. And it doesn’t bend to threats or tantrums from a would-be strongman. America isn’t about loyalty to one man, it’s about loyalty to the Constitution. Defending that is something I will never shy away from. ****[**If you believe in that too, stand with me right now. Chip in to Able Dems and me to help me keep fighting for our Constitution, our democracy, and the American Dream →**](https://click.actionnetwork.org/ss/c/u001.iIBo0N5fSFzEFL40Tn-vtbMETCUYClkOrOh9-SNJfqtHtWNDtXR0WReOmqZcCOXObfMgaGY5raGLc1PxOT-O68TdeN6kJLZ6Ix4mjuuc63D0sOK3avlwqBSexXr2jDfmcYqYGdvgL5GVarJbwREheudSbPje6Ke4ObJaIDeRWRW17UI2pTSRwAfsnpuEvQTD1PIEaTfJ7lyWX4TlUxfLMklEGxDoPI1UjecDEmQ2mIkg5HKLGMHluJQUGod-YbJhAOMwrlt-2t62l345rXyKvCjkRH_0xRH_p3AZeJ-6dFQJh_Oyp81E0jtJPNDZ8Cq4wEqnhrW4ly8cGuOIvPpVqh9AbtV-mvpSUHYecE4-HaVDnvvjDo5I9QHZI62XFEyTUPV2-hp9keXttEJW2W_j9ryZ0EjT4ueO7lzxkQTymeIa4ggh4R3wrdyhoB4AvSAN/4o9/NwQVZu5KTU-ImEHVBzyGOw/h8/h00